# Subagent model policy

When launching Task subagents (`explore`, `generalPurpose`, `shell`, `bugbot`, `security-review`, etc.):

- **Allowed models only:** `composer-2.5`, `composer-2.5-fast`, or `grok-4.5-medium`.
- **Never use:** Opus, GPT, Sonnet, or any other model slug for subagents.
- If calling Task with an explicit `model`, it must be one of the allowed slugs above. Prefer `composer-2.5`.
- If unsure, **omit `model`** so the subagent inherits the main chat model (Composer).
- Do not parallelize implementation across subagents unless the user explicitly asks.
- Prefer implementing in the main agent thread for cohesive multi-file features.

`explore` subagents already use Composer 2.5 by default — keep using them for codebase search only.
